# SOS2FA recovery code (break-glass, s3.1.3)

Why: SOS2FA codes travel only by SendGrid email and Twilio SMS. Both accounts were unpaid (Oct 2026), locking the owner out of Entity Management. SOS2FA was **not** suspended; a second factor the owner controls was added.

## Contract

- Callable `verifySos2faRecoveryCode({recoveryCode})` in `functions/sos2fa-functions.js`; pure helpers in `sos2fa-core.js` (`recoveryWindowOpen`, `recoveryCodeMatches`, `nextRecoveryAttempt`).
- Secret `SOS2FA_RECOVERY_CODE` in Secret Manager, set by the owner with `firebase functions:secrets:set` (never in chat, git, or `.env`). Under 12 characters never matches.
- Only `SUPER_ADMIN_EMAILS` (not `users.superAdmin`) with `email_verified === true`.
- Hard expiry `RECOVERY_UNTIL_ISO = "2026-10-16T04:00:00Z"` in code. Extending is a code change + deploy.
- Throttle `sos2faRecoveryAttempts/{uid}`: 5 per hour (transaction), reset on success. Rules: no client access.
- Success writes a normal `sos2faSessions` doc (`scope: entityManagement`, `via: "recovery-code"`, 1 h). Audit actions: `sos2fa_recovery_verified` / `_failed` / `_denied`.
- UI: `master-admin.html` SOS2FA gate `<details class="sos2fa-recovery">` → `sos2fa.js` `verifyRecoveryCode`.
- s3.1.28 (Oct 9 2026 owner decision): the normal Request SOS2FA Code / Verify path is open to **any Master Admin** (claim or verified listed email), not only the Super Admin. The recovery box follows the server and is shown only when `canUseRecoveryCode` (listed email + `emailVerified`) — claim holders with an unverified email (e.g. don.b, Microsoft) use the emailed code instead.

## Removal (when SendGrid / Twilio are paid)

Delete the callable + export + UI + helpers, then `firebase functions:delete verifySos2faRecoveryCode` and `firebase functions:secrets:destroy SOS2FA_RECOVERY_CODE`. Long-term replacement: TOTP authenticator (`sos2faTotp/{uid}` rule is reserved, not built).
